      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-240529",
      ":question/problem": "$B$ is the midpoint of the segment $PQ^(\u2015)$, $C$ is a point equidistant from the points $P$ and $Q$, and $l$ is the line that passes through points $C$ and $B$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$l$ is the perpendicular bisector of the segment $PQ^(\u2015)$*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of this statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | $CP = CQ$ | Given |\n| 2 | $CP^(\u2015)\u2245CQ^(\u2015)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| 3 | $PB = BQ$ | Definition of midpoint |\n| 4 | $PB^(\u2015)\u2245BQ^(\u2015)$ | Definition of congruent segments |\n| 5 | $CB^(\u2015)\u2245CB^(\u2015)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 6 | $\u25b3CPB\u2245\u25b3CQB$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 7 | $\u2220CBP\u2245\u2220CBQ$ | CPCTC |\n| 8 | $l\u22a5PQ^(\u2015)$ | Linear pair perpendicular theorem |\n| 9 | $l$ is the perpendicular bisector of $PQ^(\u2015)$ | Definition of perpendicular bisector |"
    },
